WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:39.750
A working agreement people can use In this learning activity, you will build a clear support partnership. You will identify the limits of your own authority and practise using sound judgement when requests compete. You will also learn to prepare work that meets agreed requirements and to check that another person has actually accepted any cover assignment. Translate priorities into reliable support deliverables. Distinguish EA coordination from executive and specialist decisions. Prepare a working agreement and a reasoned priority brief. Keep uncertainty visible, rather than inventing approval.
